# HEARTBEAT — Orchestrator

On every heartbeat, run:

```bash
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/digest.py
```

Then:

1. If `overdue > 0` or `urgent > 0` → message the user with a short summary (1 line per card, max 5 lines).
2. If `stale_7d > 0` → mention in the same message but don't alarm.
3. If `claimed` includes any agent whose session is dead (not seen recently) → run `release_my_claims.py <that-agent>` to free those cards.
4. If nothing notable → reply `HEARTBEAT_OK` (OpenClaw will suppress it; you won't bother the user).

Do not create cards in the heartbeat unless the digest reveals a card that needs an automatic action (e.g. archive). Card creation is reactive to user messages.

## Cheat sheet of one-liners

```bash
# what's going on
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/digest.py

# release stuck claims for an agent
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/release_my_claims.py executor

# nightly archive (already runs on its own cron, this is for ad-hoc cleanup)
# sweeps done-labelled cards off the board so each agent column stays compact
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/archive_old.py --days 14
```

Full protocol: `~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/SKILL.md`.
